request.description:
Not called by the backend adapter — included so you can inspect a full entity once search gives you a QID.

`props=labels|descriptions|claims` keeps the payload small. `claims` (a.k.a. statements) is where `P31` (instance of) / `P279` (subclass of) live — useful when deciding what `entityType` / category a piece of content should get.

Response shape:
```json
{
  "entities": {
    "Q223522": {
      "id": "Q223522",
      "labels":       { "en": { "language": "en", "value": "Kansas City Chiefs" } },
      "descriptions": { "en": { "language": "en", "value": "National Football League franchise..." } },
      "claims": { "P31": [ { "mainsnak": { "datavalue": { "value": { "id": "Q17156793" } } } } ] }
    }
  },
  "success": 1
}
```

